{"id":"pit","name":"Pit","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:pit"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Pit","text":"A hole in the ground (Ex. 21:33, 34), a cistern for water (Gen. 37:24; Jer. 14:3), a vault (41:9), a grave (Ps. 30:3). It is used as a figure for mischief (Ps. 9:15), and is the name given to the unseen place of woe (Rev. 20:1, 3). The slime-pits in the vale of Siddim were wells which yielded asphalt (Gen. 14:10)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G12","lemma":"ἄβυσσος","xlit":"ábyssos","gloss":"depthless","kjv":"deep, pit","count":6,"share":0.32},{"strong":"H3738","lemma":"כָּרָה","xlit":"kârâh","gloss":"to dig","kjv":"dig, make, open","count":4,"share":0.21},{"strong":"H5307","lemma":"נָפַל","xlit":"nâphal","gloss":"to fall, in a great variety of applications","kjv":"be accepted, cast, out), cease","count":6,"share":0.32},{"strong":"H7882","lemma":"שִׁיחָה","xlit":"shîychâh","gloss":"a pit-fall","kjv":"pit","count":2,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H953","lemma":"בּוֹר","xlit":"bôwr","gloss":"a pit hole","kjv":"cistern, dungeon, fountain, pit","count":3,"share":0.16},{"strong":"G305","lemma":"ἀναβαίνω","xlit":"anabaínō","gloss":"to go up","kjv":"arise, ascend, climb  up, come","count":3,"share":0.16}],"verses":["Rev.9.1","Rev.9.2","Rev.9.11","Rev.11.7","Rev.20.1","Rev.20.3","2Sam.23.20","Ps.7.15","Ps.7.16","Ps.40.2","Ps.57.6","Ps.69.15","Ps.119.85","Prov.23.27","Prov.26.27","Prov.28.10","Eccl.10.8","Jer.48.44","Rev.17.8"],"related":[{"id":"trumpet","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.021,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"}],"works":[]}
